      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "We have the system of equations:\n\\begin{align*}\n4u - 5v &= 23 \\tag{1} \\\\\n2u + 4v &= -8 \\tag{2}\n\\end{align*}\n\nTo eliminate one variable, we can multiply equation (2) by 2 to make the coefficients of $u$ in both equations equal:\n\\begin{align*}\n2(2u + 4v) &= 2(-8) \\\\\n4u + 8v &= -16 \\tag{3}\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow we subtract equation (3) from equation (1):\n\\begin{align*}\n(4u - 5v) - (4u + 8v) &= 23 - (-16) \\\\\n4u - 5v - 4u - 8v &= 23 + 16 \\\\\n-13v &= 39 \\\\\nv &= -3\n\\end{align*}\n\nSubstituting $v = -3$ into equation (2):\n\\begin{align*}\n2u + 4(-3) &= -8 \\\\\n2u - 12 &= -8 \\\\\n2u &= 4 \\\\\nu &= 2\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, $u + v = 2 + (-3) = \\boxed{-1}$.",
