      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve for \\(u\\) and \\(v\\), we can use the method of elimination. First, we will eliminate \\(v\\) by multiplying the first equation by 4 and the second equation by 5, and then adding them together.\n\nFirst equation: \\(4u - 5v = 23\\)\nSecond equation: \\(2u + 4v = -8\\)\n\nMultiply the first equation by 4:\n\\[4(4u - 5v) = 4(23)\\]\n\\[16u - 20v = 92\\]\n\nMultiply the second equation by 5:\n\\[5(2u + 4v) = 5(-8)\\]\n\\[10u + 20v = -40\\]\n\nNow, add these two equations together:\n\\[16u - 20v + 10u + 20v = 92 - 40\\]\n\\[26u = 52\\]\n\\[u = \\frac{52}{26}\\]\n\\[u = 2\\]\n\nNow that we have \\(u = 2\\), we can substitute this value back into one of the original equations to find \\(v\\). We'll use the second equation:\n\\[2u + 4v = -8\\]\n\\[2(2) + 4v = -8\\]\n\\[4 + 4v = -8\\]\n\\[4v = -8 - 4\\]\n\\[4v = -12\\]\n\\[v = \\frac{-12}{4}\\]\n\\[v = -3\\]\n\nNow that we have \\(u = 2\\) and \\(v = -3\\), we can find \\(u + v\\):\n\\[u + v = 2 + (-3) = -1\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(u + v\\) is \\(\\boxed{-1}\\).",
